      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/washington_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew into a key frontier outpost, helping trade and settlement in southwestern Arkansas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/washington_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Washington was a major stop on the rugged Southwest Trail, drawing pioneers heading to Texas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Civil War, Washington briefly served as the Confederate state capital from 1863 to 1865.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
